/**
@page deepdives Deep dives

@brief Mechanism guides - how a specific part actually works, in detail.

These dive into one mechanism each, past the orientation @ref overviews.

- @subpage md_docs_2SCHEDULER__PERF - **Scheduler & perf monitoring.** The
  non-blocking fixed-period loop, overrun handling, and the self-instrumented
  CPU / jitter / stack metrics.
- @subpage md_docs_2PLC__SYNC - **PLC shared-memory sync.** The RX/TX state
  machines and the transactional handshake with the PLC coprocessor.
- @subpage md_docs_2PLC__CONFIG - **PLC configuration variables and components.** The
  generic network / NTP / MQTT / geo config the PLC publishes, how to set up the
  matching PLC-side structure, and the Component / ConfigHandler-based network stack
  and sun tracker that consume it.
- @subpage md_docs_2EDITOR__RECONCILE - **Editor reconciliation.** How the line
  editor repaints a multi-row edit with the fewest bytes over the serial link.
*/
